{"np_t15" "The 75 mm Gun Motor Carriage M3 was a United States tank destroyer and self-propelled artillery piece of World War II. It was the most numerous tank destroyer in United States Army service during the critical battles in North Africa and the Philippines; and continued to be used in more limited numbers in Sicily, before being declared obsolete in early 1944. The GMC M3 was then used by the regimental weapons companies of Marine regiments in 1944-1945 at Saipan, Peleliu and Okinawa."}
; -- group d7 --
; [new] card "m3stuart_early" cost 280 lvl 1 | soldiers tankman x3, tankman2 | tags all 42 | units/usa/vehicles_42.set:57
{"m3stuart_early"  "The M3 was the logical advancement of the M2. The armour was increased, the chassis and the turret were modified from insights of armoured battles of 1939-40. In 1940 the M3 was accepted and entered production in 1941 at American Car & Foundry. While in production the turret was replaced with a more roundened version without riveted armour plates. Due to delivery problems, 500 M3 were supplied with the Guiberson T-1020 Diesel engines instead of the Standard Gasoline engine from Continental."}
